div.p:
The domestic exports of the United States during the past year were as follows:
                    Cotton, $192,000,000; grain, $33,000,000; wheat, $68,000,000; Hour, $24,000,000;
                    other articles, $80,000,000.

The imports of manufactured articles: Cotton, $20,000,000; flax, $15,000,000;
                    iron and steel, $10,000,000; silk, $22,000,000; sugar, $71,000,000; wool and
                    manufactures, $38,000,000.
